# Citation metadata for agentic-bioinspired-cad (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# Lets GitHub render a "Cite this repository" button and gives users a precise,
# machine-readable citation. Update `version` / `date-released` on each tagged
# release (the release workflow refuses a tag whose version disagrees).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "agentic-bioinspired-cad"
abstract: >-
  A fully local agentic LLM-to-CAD-to-FEA-to-print loop for single-material,
  damage-tolerant, 3D-printable bioinspired architectures. Parametric generators
  for helicoidal (Bouligand), woven-lattice and enamel-decussation families are
  coupled to a closed design loop (code-emitting language model, headless Blender
  build and render, schema-constrained vision critic, repair agents and a
  manufacturability gate) and to verification instruments: a printability audit,
  voxel-hex linear and finite-strain finite-element analysis, a flaw-seeded
  damage-tolerance retention metric, and MOOSE phase-field fracture simulations
  of crack twisting and deflection.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Renteria"
    given-names: "Cameron B."
    email: "crentb23@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "University of Washington"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/crentb/agentic-bioinspired-cad"
keywords:
  - "bioinspired design"
  - "architected materials"
  - "damage tolerance"
  - "Bouligand"
  - "woven lattice"
  - "tooth enamel"
  - "generative CAD"
  - "large language models"
  - "agentic workflow"
  - "finite element analysis"
  - "phase-field fracture"
  - "additive manufacturing"
# Work this software builds on: the code emitter is the Bioinspired3D LoRA adapter, and the
# emit, render, critique and repair loop follows the Bioinspired123D system it was released with.
